     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've logged the run as UNKNOWN because the growth stage requires a tube pressure gauge and this furnace doesn't have one. Without it I can't confirm the tube atmosphere.\n\n- **Normal so far:** temperature followed the ramp and settled at about 750 °C, with a brief overshoot to 760.4 °C at the start of growth. Argon flow held at about 100 sccm, heater power was steady at about 44–45%, and exhaust oxygen stayed at about 3–5 ppm after the purge.\n- **What the missing gauge hides:** low oxygen argues against a leak letting air in. But a blocked exhaust or over-pressure mainly shows up as a pressure change, so the oxygen reading can't rule those out.\n- **Sample result:** the sample hasn't been characterized yet, so there's no evidence either way on whether the material grew.\n\nI've proposed calling a person to take a pressure reading, either with a manual gauge or a temporarily fitted sensor, while growth is still going. If that reading is normal, the run can be treated as normal."
     }
    ],
